data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/mission_summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission summary: greet, tested\\n\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` defines `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covers a normal name (`greet(\\\"Alice\\\")`) and the\\n   empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\")`).\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 (2 tests, OK).\\n\\ndev delivered this correctly on its first dispatch (d002), committed to its\\nown branch (`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit `0a4b10d`).\\nI independently verified by fetching that branch and running the test suite\\nmyself in an isolated worktree (not dev's working copy) — confirmed 2 tests\\npassed with exit code 0, and that the commit touched only the two required\\nfiles. No rework was necessary. Full report at\\n~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/report.md.\\n\\nNothing is unmet.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

